  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Wahda Kabira (\"kabira\" is Arabic for large), also known as Wahda Sunbati, is a stretched out version of Iqa‘ Wahda over two measures. It is very popular in the vocal and instrumental music of the mid-twentieth century."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Wahda Kabira 8/4 (also called Wahda Sunbati) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Wahda Kabira Pronunciation of Wahda Sunbati Iqa‘ Wahda Kabira (\"kabira\" is Arabic for large), also known as Wahda Sunbati , is a stretched out version of Iqa‘ Wahda over two measures. It is very popular in the vocal and instrumental music of the mid-twentieth century. Khatwit Habibi (1953) Instrumental by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Habibi Yis‘id Awqatu (1943) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) il-Albi Yi‘shaq Kulli Gamil (1961) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Tuta (1942) Instrumental Composition (from the movie Ahlam el-Shabab ) Music by Farid al-Atrash Ya Bid‘ el-Ward (1944) Asmahan Music by Farid al-Atrash Tile‘ Li el-Biki Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Sawa Rbina (1968) Fairouz Music by the Rahbani Brothers Iqa‘ Wahda Kabira 8/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
